"""Rasterise the social icons shipped in `prblm_mailer/static/prblm_mailer/icons/`.

**Development-only.** Run it when the icon set changes; the package itself ships the
resulting PNGs and never needs cairosvg at runtime:

    pip install cairosvg
    python scripts/build_icons.py

PNG, not SVG, because Gmail strips SVG entirely. Two variants per platform (white
and dark glyph) and no coloured variants: the block colours the *chip* behind the
glyph with an inline background, which every client renders, and picks whichever
glyph contrasts with it.

Icon sources: brand marks from Simple Icons (CC0, simpleicons.org), except LinkedIn
(Simple Icons removed it at LinkedIn's request) which is the Font Awesome mark, and
`email`/`website`, drawn here because they aren't anybody's brand. The listed brand
colour is only the default chip colour when the editor picks none.
"""
